      {
        "id": 82217,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-11-21T12:56:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>The discard effect has to trigger for police backup's \"would discard\" to take effect.</p><p>For example if Fixer was highest HP hero vs. Matriarch and a fowl was destroyed, and Fixer chose to destroy a card he would not get to redirect the damage that he would have taken if he hadn't destroyed a card.</p><p>In Police Backup's case you would have to choose the discard effect if it was optional for Backup to be destroyed.</p><p>If you get a \"discard your hand\" and a hero has 0 cards in hand and they choose to discard their hand of zero cards police backup would be destroyed because they would have discarded.</p><p>This is how I interpret Police Backup.</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:04:54.322Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
